From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Mihalicka <tomas@mihalicka.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Cache payments per tenant

Every payment lookup takes the payment log's lock and reads from disk,
so a lookup waits for other tenants' disk reads and for every save's
sync to disk. Clients poll a payment right after creating it, so most
of those reads are for a few recent payments.

Keep recently saved and read payments in memory, behind a lock that is
only ever held for in-memory work. Each tenant gets its own bounded
space, sized by PAYMENTS_CACHE_PER_TENANT, so one busy tenant cannot
evict another tenant's payments; within a tenant the oldest entry goes
first. Saves write through to the cache. A payment read from the log is
cached only if no copy is there yet, so a read racing a save cannot put
an older state back.

Areas: scalability, infrastructure
